-- title:
--   Crossing chart coordinate minus its value is a uniformiser
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ contain every unit whose image under reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is trivial, and let `hj` witness $\mathrm{jqModC}\ \mathbb{Q} \in \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`: a proper, flat, integral, locally finitely presented two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ over $R\,p$, normal on affine opens, equipped with a curve model `Meta` of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an isomorphism `𝔛.eeta` of `Meta.C` with the base change of the model along $R\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, satisfying the Galois-equivariance, chart-pinning and generic-fibre conditions of that structure. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R\,p \to A$ inducing $\mathrm{algebraMap}$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R\,p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, and maps $\mathrm{to\kappa} : O \to \kappa_A$, $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\iota_A : O \to A$ compatible with $\rho$, $\rho_O$, the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and reduction. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 0$ and $\dots 1$, and write $x_n$ for the image of $n$ in $X_O :=$ the base change of the model along $\rho_O$ under the first projection followed by the $0$-component and `bcMap`. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U$ be an open of $X_O$ containing $x_n$, and let $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec} Q$, $Q = \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ O\ (p^{e}) = O[x_0,x_1]/(x_0x_1 - p^{e})$, be a chart over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ (i.e. $f$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $O \to Q$ equals $U.\iota$ followed by the structure morphism), subject to: both distinguished classes `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` lie in $f(y)$ exactly when $y$ maps to $x_n$; at such $y$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and is an isomorphism on residue fields, and $f$ is étale on some open neighbourhood of $y$; and the vanishing of `CrossingQuotient.V` (resp. `CrossingQuotient.U`) at $y$ is equivalent to $y$ lying in the image of the $0$-component (resp. $1$-component) composed with `bcMap`. Write $\mathrm{pr}_J$ for the map from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ to $X_O$ induced by $j_O$, let $g_v$, $g_u$ be the sections of $X_O$ over $U.\iota\,''\,\top$ obtained by pulling back the classes `CrossingQuotient.V`, `CrossingQuotient.U` along $f$, and, for any proof that the generic point of `Meta.C` lies in the preimage of $U.\iota\,''\,\top$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_J$, let $\mathrm{read}$ be the ring homomorphism from sections on $U.\iota\,''\,\top$ to $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H$ given by pulling back along $\mathrm{pr}_J$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, taking the germ at the generic point, and transporting by `Meta.ffEquiv.symm`; put $\mathrm{param} := \mathrm{read}\ g_v$. Then for every place $W$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $A$-point $s$ of $U$ lying over $\operatorname{Spec} \iota_A$, whose generic fibre is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X_O$ attached to $W$ through `Meta.pointEquivPlace` and whose closed point maps to $x_n$, and every ring homomorphism $\chi : Q \to A$ with $s$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec} \chi$, one has $\mathrm{ord}_W\bigl(\mathrm{param} - \chi(\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.V}\ (p^{e}))\bigr) = 1$, where the value of $\chi$ is viewed in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and then in the function field, and $\mathrm{ord}_W$ is minus the logarithm of the adic valuation of $W$.
--
--   This is the statement that on the annulus attached to a crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model, the chart coordinate minus its value at a point is a uniformiser at the corresponding place of the function field: the difference $\mathrm{param} - \chi(V)$ has order exactly $1$ at every rational place $W$ whose section passes through the crossing. It feeds the construction of the annulus parametrisation in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_annulus_mem_dom_iff_and_param_eq_read_chart_and_modulus_eq_pow_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_annulus_mem_dom_iff_and_param_eq_read_chart_and_modulus_eq_pow_of_chart_of_residue_surjective).
